course: dictionary
lesson: 14042
title: Making, or making up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Manufacture is a word with two main jobs. The first is about making things in large numbers, usually in a factory with machines. «The factory can manufacture 200 bikes each day.» Here the factory makes bikes, lots of them, every day.
explain: As a noun, manufacture means the making of goods. «The town is famous for the manufacture of cars» tells you that the town makes cars. Look for the little words around it, like «of», which often show that the word is a noun.
explain: The second job is more surprising. To manufacture an excuse or a story means to invent it, often a false one. «Sam tried to manufacture an excuse for being late.» Sam did not find a real reason; he made one up. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "make up" fit? Then you have it.
fact: Manufacture means to make goods in large numbers, usually in a factory with machines.
fact: «Manufactured goods» are things that have been made in a factory.
fact: «Manufacture» as a noun means the making of goods, as in «the manufacture of cars».
fact: «To manufacture an excuse» means to invent a false reason, as in «He manufactured a story about the dog eating his homework».
fact: A "date of manufacture" printed on packaging tells you when the item was made.
exercise: «The factory can manufacture 200 bikes each day.» What does manufacture mean here? | Sell bikes to shops | Ride bikes around the town | Repair old bikes slowly | *Make goods in large numbers
exercise: On a tin, the label says «Date of manufacture: May 2023». What does manufacture mean? | The day it was bought | Repair | Throwing away | *The making of the goods
exercise: «Sam tried to manufacture an excuse for being late.» What does manufacture mean here? | Hide the bus ticket | *Invent a false story | Post a letter | Finish
test: «The town's main industry is the manufacture of cars.» What does manufacture mean? | Driving cars | Selling old cars | Parking cars | *The making of goods
test: «The machines manufacture shoes all day.» What does the words all day tell you? | The shoes are being sold | The machines are resting | The machines have broken down | *The machines keep making shoes for hours
exam: Rosa says manufacture always means build a house. What is the best answer? | Yes, always | *No, it can mean making goods in large numbers, or inventing a false excuse | No, it means to sleep | Yes, but only in maths lessons
